+### 9d. Decision — no speculation on the live entry (pending A/prod)
+
+Rule: deploy only if speculation improves real traffic with both slots busy.
+
+- Greedy dual-agent fg: off 26.3, A 25.5 (26.1 without length rows), B 23.0
+  tok/s. Greedy dual-mem fg: off 25.0, A 23.8, B 22.4. Neither ngram setting
+  is faster than off with both slots busy; A is the only spec arm not fully
+  dominated, but it is slower.
+- A's single-agent "86.0 tok/s" is an artifact: two rows hit max_tokens under
+  spec-induced greedy loops (mem0-r0/0/2, mem0-r2/0/2) while off finished both
+  normally with tool_calls (1020 and 3701 tokens). Excluding length rows A is
+  54.3 tok/s vs off 56.2. Loops are a quality regression, not a speedup.
+- Spec is the worse arm on normally-finishing turns in every phase (greedy,
+  no-length rows): single-agent 55.0 (B) / 54.3 (A) vs off 56.2; dual-mem 22.4 /
+  23.8 vs 25.0; mem 50.7 / 53.1 vs 55.6.
+- Quality: spec changes temperature-0 outputs even with draft_n = 0
+  (baseline-r0/0/0: 530c... off vs cdad... A vs f20f... B, all 71 tok).
+  Same-sha share vs off (fg): single-agent A 3/30 B 2/30; single-mem 10/12 both;
+  dual-agent 0/30 both; dual-mem 11/12 both.
+- MMproj outcome: no refusal on text-only traffic with --mmproj/--no-mmproj-offload
+  — A and B servers run fine and produce drafts (A fg draft_n>0 in
+  single-agent 3/30 rows, single-mem, dual-agent; B 1/30 in single-agent, 1/12
+  in single-mem, 1/30 dual-agent). Per server-context.cpp:3550-3553, image input
+  with spec on is untested/risky (`unsupported batch.has_embd + spec`), so even
+  if spec helped text-only, the production entry serves vision-traffic-prone
+  agent turns; untested with --mmproj.
+- Checkpoint evidence: 0 'restore checkpoint' / 'will use checkpoints' lines in
+  any A/B server log. 'will use checkpoints' is logged at SRV_TRC (server-context.cpp:1172),
+  so its absence from the replay logs (default verbosity) is expected, not a
+  signal that speculation was off — drafts were produced instead.
+- VRAM: 9507 MiB / 10240 MiB used after the first fg request for off and A
+  (all four phases), no observable increase from ngram-mod drafting in this setup.
+- prod base (off-prod) dual-agent fg 31.2 (32.6 no-length) tok/s is the number
+  A/prod must beat for a change of heart; the rule itself is set on dual-agent
+  greedy and A does not beat off there.
